\details{
The algorithm explores a union of parameter spaces indexed by which subsets
of positions from a user-supplied \strong{maximal} \code{mrfi} are active. A position
is \emph{active} when its corresponding \code{theta} entries are non-zero; the current
active set is tracked via an \code{included} logical vector of length equal to
the number of positions in the maximal \code{mrfi}.

At each iteration one of five moves is proposed:
\describe{
\item{\code{within}}{Random-walk perturbation of the active \code{theta} entries.}
\item{\code{birth}}{Add a randomly chosen inactive position (draw its \code{theta}
from a \code{N(0, sdbirth^2)} proposal, with a conservative redistribution
of that value back to currently active positions).}
\item{\code{death}}{Remove a randomly chosen active position (set its \code{theta}
to zero, redistributing the removed mass to the remaining active
positions).}
\item{\code{swap}}{Move the \code{theta} values from one active position to a
randomly chosen inactive one (model dimension unchanged).}
\item{\code{jump}}{Toggle a randomly chosen position: if active, zero it out;
if inactive, add it with a fresh \code{N(0, sdbirth^2)} draw.}
}

The log pseudo-posterior target is:
\deqn{\log \tilde\pi(\theta, M | z) =
  \log PL(z|\theta) + \sum_{k \in M} \log\phi(\theta_k; 0, \sigma_{\rm prior})
  - \lambda |M|}
where \eqn{M} is the active set, \eqn{|M|} is its cardinality, and
\eqn{\lambda = \log(nm)} is a BIC-like penalty.
}
